{
  "project": "Pokemon Mercury Redux",
  "date": "2026-09-05",
  "scope": "Post-Candice Mt. Coronet ascent + B1F Feebas lake + Spear Pillar encounter policy",
  "status": "STAGED_FOR_FINAL_SINNOH_MAPS",
  "design_source": "Pokemon Platinum / Sinnoh, expanded for Mercury Redux",
  "source_rule": "Platinum/Sinnoh defines geography, encounter anchors, ecology, and progression. Emerald-derived engine IDs are hidden implementation infrastructure only and are not content sources.",
  "runtime_note": "The cumulative source does not yet contain the finished player-facing Platinum-derived upper Mt. Coronet / Spear Pillar maps. These are authoritative staged encounter specifications and must only be wired when those real Sinnoh maps exist.",
  "design_rules": [
    "Preserve Platinum Mt. Coronet anchors such as Clefairy, Golbat, Machoke, Graveler, Nosepass, Medicham, Chingling/Chimecho, Bronzong, Snover, and Abomasnow.",
    "Different Coronet floors must have distinct sub-identities rather than cloning one cave roster at higher levels.",
    "The snowy mountainside uses Morning/Day/Evening/Night turnover because it is outdoors.",
    "B1F Feebas lake keeps Feebas tied to Mt. Coronet but removes the tiny-tile lottery; Feebas is a permanent rare fishing target.",
    "Spear Pillar has no generic random wild encounter table; story/static legendary encounters remain scripted content."
  ],
